{"text":"The second type of aid is what I would call NGO or charitable aid, and think of this as relatively small amounts of money that we give, you know, $10 to buy a mosquito net in Zambia or, you know, $15 to Kenya to send a girl to school. I myself am involved in a number of charities, but the fact of the matter is, let us not delude ourselves. This type of intervention is not going to miraculously make Africa grow at the level of economic growth that it needs to grow to reduce poverty and create jobs. By the way, I should remind you that over 60% of Africans are under the age of 24. In many countries in Africa, over 50% of the population is under the age of 15. So we've got a very, very young population. We need to create jobs. We don't need pity. We don't need sympathy. We need jobs. And here it's really important to remember that, yes, you can send €10 to a child in Ghana, and maybe she will go to school, but if the economies are not growing fast enough, when she graduates, she will not be able to get a job.","words":[{"text":"The","start":0.0,"end":0.68},{"text":"second","start":0.68,"end":0.92},{"text":"type","start":0.92,"end":1.18},{"text":"of","start":1.18,"end":1.32},{"text":"aid","start":1.32,"end":1.56},{"text":"is","start":1.56,"end":1.92},{"text":"what","start":1.92,"end":2.48},{"text":"I","start":2.48,"end":2.58},{"text":"would","start":2.58,"end":2.7},{"text":"call","start":2.7,"end":2.9},{"text":"NGO","start":2.9,"end":3.44},{"text":"or","start":3.44,"end":3.72},{"text":"charitable","start":3.72,"end":4.14},{"text":"aid","start":4.14,"end":4.54,"punct":","},{"text":"and","start":4.7,"end":4.7},{"text":"think","start":4.7,"end":4.86},{"text":"of","start":4.86,"end":5.02},{"text":"this","start":5.02,"end":5.2},{"text":"as","start":5.2,"end":5.38},{"text":"relatively","start":5.38,"end":5.88},{"text":"small","start":5.88,"end":6.46},{"text":"amounts","start":6.46,"end":6.78},{"text":"of","start":6.78,"end":7.04},{"text":"money","start":7.04,"end":7.